          "deepDive": "**〜をめぐって** comes from 巡る *to go around*: many people, opinions or interests *revolve around* one issue. The key image is **several parties + one contested topic**.\n\nSo the predicate is almost always a word of debate or conflict: 議論する・論争・対立する・争う・もめる・意見が分かれる・話し合う・さまざまな憶測が飛ぶ. The noun before it is the issue: 遺産, 建設計画, 増税, 領土, 移転, 〜の是非 (*whether ~ is right*).\n\n- **をめぐって / をめぐり** link clauses (めぐり is more written).\n- **をめぐる + N** modifies a noun: 基地移転をめぐる問題, 相続をめぐるトラブル.\n\nHow it differs from について / に関して:\n- **について / に関して** simply mark a topic: 日本の歴史について本を読む. Anyone can talk *about* something alone.\n- **をめぐって** implies interaction and disagreement. ✗日本の歴史をめぐって本を読む sounds wrong — reading a book is not a dispute.\n- **に対して** marks the target of an attitude or action: 上司に対して不満がある. It's the person/thing you face, not the issue people argue over.\n\nRegister: it is a newspaper word. Headlines love it: 「新球場建設をめぐり住民が反発」.\n\nJLPT tip: when you see 対立, 議論, 争い, 意見が分かれる later in the sentence and the blank follows the disputed issue, choose をめぐって. If the noun is a *standard* or *source* (法律, データ), think に基づいて (#138) instead.",
