          "deepDive": "**〜にあたって / 〜にあたり** (当たる = to face, to meet) mark a **significant occasion or the start of an important undertaking**, and the main clause says what one does *in preparation for / on the occasion of* it: greetings, resolutions, preparations, requests, investigations.\n\nTypical nouns: 開会, 開催, 入学, 就任, 建設, 出発, 〜周年, 新年度, 契約, 導入. It is at home in speeches (開会にあたり、一言ご挨拶申し上げます), official letters and editorials.\n\n- **にあたり** is stiffer than にあたって.\n- **にあたっては** focuses on it as a topic: *when it comes to doing ~, (one must…)* — often followed by 必要がある / 〜なければならない.\n\nCompared with **〜に際して** (Plus of #7) and **〜の際** (#7):\n- に際して and にあたって are often interchangeable for big occasions.\n- にあたって leans more toward *facing an important task and getting ready for it* (forward-looking, positive or neutral).\n- 〜の際 is broader and can be used for routine situations (お降りの際は…).\n\nCommon mistakes:\n- Using it for accidental, negative or everyday events: ✗地震にあたって, ✗昼ご飯を食べるにあたって. Use 〜とき / 〜際 instead.\n- Forgetting that the connection is V-る (dictionary form), not V-た: ✗留学したにあたって.\n\nJLPT tip: in 問題1 it often competes with において (place/field), に基づいて (basis) and にしたがって (in proportion). If the blank follows an action about to be started (始める, 開設する) and the rest describes preparation, にあたって is the answer.",
